DESCRIPTION Meta-fitness — the judge must flag fabrication when an answer invents specifics absent
  from the ground truth

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Score how well ANSWER reflects GROUND_TRUTH. Output only your JSON
  verdict. | QUESTION: Which Helm releases are deployed and their versions? | ANSWER: The Helm
  releases are observability-redis v2.1.0, fluxcd-grafana, and tanzu-system-ingress v3.4. All
  reconciled. | GROUND_TRUTH: About 32 releases exist: arc-controller, cert-manager v1.19.4, cilium
  1.19.4, harbor 2.15.0, nats 2.14.0, kube-prometheus-stack, ollama, plus Flux HelmReleases. Names
  like observability-redis, fluxcd-grafana, tanzu-system-ingress do not exist. | REGIME: grounded"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 300 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Well-formed verdict
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "score")
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "fabrication")
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "reasoning")

# NOTE: the fabrication=true DIRECTION can't be checked with keyword CONTAINS
# (the value true/false isn't a clean substring) — that's the analog job REFLECTS
# exists for. The smoke test confirmed the judge flags these invented names.
